	(text_box "Notes\n1. MCU supplies per ST AN6011: 100 nF at each VDD (19, 33, 64), VDDSMPS (29), VDDUSB (48), VBAT (1); 10 uF bulk; 10 uF at VDDSMPS.\n2. SMPS: L1 2.2 uH from VLXSMPS (28) to VDD11 (31, 62); 2 x 2.2 uF + 100 nF on VDD11 to VSSSMPS (30). VDD11 ~0.9 V: core only, no external loads.\n3. LQFP64 has no VREF+ pin (bonded to VDDA). VDDA via FB1 + 1 uF + 100 nF. AREF on the Uno header connects to VDDA only if JP3 is closed.\n4. Use the SMPS (Q) part only: STM32U385RGT6Q / STM32U375RGT6Q. Non-Q LQFP64 has different power pins (pin 32 is VDD there).\n5. Crystals per AN2867: CL1 = CL2 = 2 (CL - Cstray). LSE 32.768 kHz 7 pF -> 8.2 pF. HSE 16 MHz is optional (USB runs from HSI48).\n6. BQ25185: R20 18k -> 4.2 V / ILIM 500 mA; R21 1k -> 300 mA; R22 10k -> TS disabled. +3V3 from TLV75733P on VSYS. +5V on USB power only.\n7. I2C1 PB6/PB7: LP5009 0x14, OLED 0x3C, SHT45 0x44, ADS1115 0x48. SPI1 PA5/6/7 shared by Uno, mikroBUS, microSD.\n8. UARTs: USART1 PA9/PA10 = D1/D0, J7, mikroBUS. USART3 PC10/PC11 = Grove UART. SWO on PB3 (J2 only); D3 = PC6. BOOT0 = PH3 (pin 60).\n9. STM32duino: board Generic U385RGTxQ; set Wire.setSDA(PB7)/setSCL(PB6); USART1 = Uart(PA_10_ALT1, PA_9_ALT1).\n10. Direct GPIO control (no I/O expander): EN_GROVE1 PC1(100k pull-down = off at reset), MIKRO_RST PC3 (10k pull-up),\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400.812 132.08 0)
		(size 170.688 72.7401)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
